        "patchSetId": 17
      },
      "lineNbr": 65,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000277
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-04-11T14:06:20Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I\u0027d prefer to have a `gpu_linux_none_stable` mixin in https://source.chromium.org/chromium/chromium/src/+/main:infra/config/targets/mixins.star and use it for Chromium SwANGLE bots, and also import it in ANGLE and Dawn.\nCurrently, these are the dimensions that SwANGLE bots use:\n```\n          \"dimensions\": {\n            \"cpu\": \"x86-64\",\n            \"gpu\": \"none\",\n            \"os\": \"Ubuntu-22.04\",\n            \"pool\": \"chromium.tests.gpu\"\n          },\n```\nI think I prefer that to `\u0027gce\u0027: \u00271\u0027` for consistency with other `gpu_*` mixins.\n\nFor now, we can use the existing mixins in waterfalls.pyl, like ANGLE does:\n```\n        \u0027mixins\u0027: [\n          \u0027gpu-swarming-pool\u0027,\n          \u0027no_gpu\u0027,\n          \u0027linux-jammy\u0027,\n          \u0027x86-64\u0027,\n        ],\n```",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 56,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 65,
        "endChar": 0
      },
      "revId": "25e55c85f268a9526d45a04a9570400ab89650e5",
      "serverId": "dd02978d-1a8e-36d7-bcc0-a5723e5c0abd"
